<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/assertion/2271649438249da50769eedc773cd91a483c4e3315a171ebc15d0842b6d85d03> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A directed graph admits a topological ordering exactly when it has no directed cycle. The input condition replaces the previous generic uses predicate."@en <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/provenance> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/assertion/2271649438249da50769eedc773cd91a483c4e3315a171ebc15d0842b6d85d03> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A total vertex ordering respecting all directed edges exists exactly when the finite directed graph is acyclic."@en <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/provenance> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/assertion/2271649438249da50769eedc773cd91a483c4e3315a171ebc15d0842b6d85d03> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Acyclicity is a condition for a topological ordering of the input directed graph. NetworkX documents this condition and raises an exception when the graph has a directed cycle."@en <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/provenance> .
