<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/probability-distributions> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "In a uniform sample of size n without replacement from m successes and N−m failures, the probability of k successes is choose(m,k) choose(N−m,n−k) divided by choose(N,n). Here 0 ≤ n ≤ N, 0 ≤ m ≤ N and max(0,n−(N−m)) ≤ k ≤ min(n,m); the mass is zero outside the support."@en <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/scheme/statistics> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Hypergeometric probability mass formula"@en <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/module/statistics/modules/interdisciplinary.ttl> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/provenance> .
