<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/vocab/uses> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/ontomath-pro-e867> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/probability-distributions> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "For a valid uniform sample without replacement, sum the count of subsets with exactly k successes over all feasible k. Vandermonde's identity gives the total number choose(N,n) of subsets of size n, so the masses sum to one."@en <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/scheme/statistics> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Vandermonde normalization of hypergeometric mass"@en <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/asserted> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/module/statistics/modules/interdisciplinary.ttl> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/graph/provenance> .
